examples.question_text:
The protractor centre is on the vertex. Its outer scale starts at zero on the right-hand arm. Read the marked angle. Each small interval is $5^{\circ}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9,every node/.style={font=\normalsize,text=black}]
\draw[black] (3,0) arc (0:180:3);
\draw[black] (-3,0)--(3,0);
\foreach \a in {0,5,...,180}{\draw[black] (\a:2.88)--(\a:3);}
\foreach \a in {0,20,...,180}{\draw[black] (\a:2.73)--(\a:3);\ifnum\a=0\node[below] at (\a:3.38) {$\a$};\else\ifnum\a=180\node[below] at (\a:3.38) {$\a$};\else\node at (\a:3.38) {$\a$};\fi\fi\pgfmathtruncatemacro{\b}{180-\a}\pgfmathtruncatemacro{\c}{mod(\a,40)}\ifnum\c=0\ifnum\a=0\node[below] at (\a:2.42) {$\b$};\else\ifnum\a=180\node[below] at (\a:2.42) {$\b$};\else\ifnum\a=60\node[anchor=north west] at (\a:2.42) {$\b$};\else\node at (\a:2.42) {$\b$};\fi\fi\fi\else\ifnum\a=180\node[below] at (\a:2.42) {$\b$};\fi\fi}
\fill[black] (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\draw[black,thick] (0,0)--(0:3.05);
\draw[black,thick] (0,0)--(65:3.05);
\draw[black] (0:0.65) arc (0:65:0.65);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The starting arm points left. Read the marked angle from the scale that starts at zero on this arm.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.9,every node/.style={font=\normalsize,text=black}]
\draw[black] (3,0) arc (0:180:3);
\draw[black] (-3,0)--(3,0);
\foreach \a in {0,5,...,180}{\draw[black] (\a:2.88)--(\a:3);}
\foreach \a in {0,20,...,180}{\draw[black] (\a:2.73)--(\a:3);\ifnum\a=0\node[below] at (\a:3.38) {$\a$};\else\ifnum\a=180\node[below] at (\a:3.38) {$\a$};\else\node at (\a:3.38) {$\a$};\fi\fi\pgfmathtruncatemacro{\b}{180-\a}\pgfmathtruncatemacro{\c}{mod(\a,40)}\ifnum\c=0\ifnum\a=0\node[below] at (\a:2.42) {$\b$};\else\ifnum\a=180\node[below] at (\a:2.42) {$\b$};\else\ifnum\a=40\node[anchor=south east] at (\a:2.42) {$\b$};\else\node at (\a:2.42) {$\b$};\fi\fi\fi\else\ifnum\a=180\node[below] at (\a:2.42) {$\b$};\fi\fi}
\fill[black] (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\draw[black,thick] (0,0)--(180:3.05);
\draw[black,thick] (0,0)--(40:3.05);
\draw[black] (40:0.65) arc (40:180:0.65);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Both marked angles are drawn to scale. Use a protractor.
(a) Measure the first angle.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8,every node/.style={font=\normalsize,text=black}]
\draw[black] (0,0)--(4,0);
\draw[black] (0,0)--(49:4);
\draw[black] (0.8,0) arc (0:49:0.8);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(b) Measure the second angle, then state which is larger.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8,every node/.style={font=\normalsize,text=black}]
\draw[black] (0,0)--(4,0);
\draw[black] (0,0)--(126:4);
\draw[black] (0.8,0) arc (0:126:0.8);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Measure the marked reflex angle. The smaller angle is drawn to scale.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8,every node/.style={font=\normalsize,text=black}]
\draw[black] (0,0)--(4,0);
\draw[black] (0,0)--(128:4);
\draw[black] (128:0.8) arc (128:360:0.8);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The starting arm is tilted. Measure the marked angle with a protractor. The diagram is drawn to scale.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[black,thick] (0,0)--(25:3.5);
\draw[black,thick] (0,0)--(105:3.5);
\draw[black] (25:0.7) arc (25:105:0.7);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Place the centre on the vertex. Turn the protractor so its zero line follows the tilted starting arm.
Read the scale that starts at zero on that arm. The other arm crosses at $80^{\circ}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\begin{scope}[rotate=25]
\draw[black] (3,0) arc (0:180:3);
\draw[black] (-3,0)--(3,0);
\foreach \a in {0,5,...,180}{\draw[black] (\a:2.88)--(\a:3);}
\foreach \a in {0,20,...,180}{\draw[black] (\a:2.72)--(\a:3);\path (\a:3.35) node {$\a$};}
\draw[black,thick] (0,0)--(3.5,0);
\draw[black,thick] (0,0)--(80:3.5);
\fill[black] (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\draw[black] (0:0.7) arc (0:80:0.7);
\path (40:1.15) node {$80^{\circ}$};
\end{scope}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
